{"Forcing refresh_token to the literal string 'refresh_token' will overwrite the real refresh token when call sites persist tokenResponse.data back to the DB (e.g. Zoom/Office365), breaking subsequent refreshes and potentially locking users out of the integration": 0.8906891942024231, "minimumTokenResponseSchema uses computed keys that evaluate to a single literal key instead of expressing 'any numeric property' in Zod, causing the schema to fail validation of real token responses and making refresh flows throw when sync is enabled": 0.8765787482261658, "refreshOAuthTokens returns a fetch Response when sync is enabled, but returns provider-specific response types otherwise (AxiosResponse, HubSpot token object, GaxiosResponse), causing call sites that access .data or assume provider-specific return shape to break when credential syncing is enabled": 0.9457451105117798, "Checking response.statusText !== 'OK' is brittle since statusText can vary and doesn't guarantee 2xx; should use response.ok or response.status for reliability and correct error status codes": 0.9311953186988831, "Webhook handler doesn't enforce HTTP method and uses schema.parse(req.body) which throws and returns 500 on invalid payloads instead of using safeParse": 0.9021563529968262, "APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED is a string/undefined value (from && of env vars) but used as a boolean flag, causing potential string leakage and unclear downstream typing": 0.7484403252601624, "req.headers[...] can be a string[] so direct equality check can incorrectly reject valid requests": 0.670945942401886}